// Two Supabase platform builds ship materially different stock objects, and remediation 28
// made managed-object fingerprints exact bytes, so a single baseline could certify only one
// of them. A target is certified against a COMPLETE profile: it must match one of these
// sets in full. It may NEVER assemble a pass by taking one object from LOCAL and another
// from HOSTED — see classifyManagedSchemaObjects.
//
// These are version-controlled positive evidence, captured from known-stock platforms.
// They are NEVER learned from the target under inspection. Regenerating one is an explicit
// maintenance operation: capture the managed-object probe output from a known-stock project
// of that shape, and update BOTH the objects and the certified digest below.
//
// Each profile's `digest` is a sha256 over its entries, each rendered as
// `schema|kind|name|owner|fingerprint`, stable-sorted, joined with one LF and no trailing
// LF. It is verified at module load, so a hand-edited entry fails closed rather than
// silently widening what counts as stock.
//
// Dynamic realtime daily partitions belong to NEITHER profile. They are date-derived and
// service-generated, so they are matched structurally by realtimePartitionDefinition().

